Hildebrandt Tower is the headquarters of the [[Org/Hildebrandt Corporation/index|Hildebrandt Corporation]] in [[Geography/Færrin/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], a skyscraper some forty floors from base to tip. It is one of the newer buildings in the city, stone and steel and glass, and its foyer rises to thirty-foot ceilings, built to tell anyone who walks in that the company has money and is better than the people who walk by.

At the back of the foyer stands a bank of paternosters, platforms that rise and fall in a continuous loop and are stepped onto as they slow. Around the twentieth floor is the ballroom, glass-walled enough to take in the aurora, with offices above it. The topmost floor holds the company vault, where gold lies in piles.

On a lockdown the tower seals itself: black metal shutters drop across the doors and archways and the paternosters stop.
